From 748a9047f6f92f2d1b8137de58f96e73783731fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:50:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] Bluetooth: btcentauri: Drop an unused variable

cen_hci_reset_dup_filter() never uses the driver data it looks up, and
clang warns about it.

Developed with Claude Code.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>

(cherry picked from commit d2476d4b3c1623306de1993a91021b7066927a6c)
[n1-wifi: on aurora-j716s this driver replaces integration's J813/J873 N1 driver files]
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btcentauri.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btcentauri.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btcentauri.c
index 42f14426a800..6f500c5e1526 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btcentauri.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btcentauri.c
@@ -580,7 +580,6 @@ static int cen_vendor_command(struct hci_dev *hdev, u16 opcode,
 
 static int cen_hci_reset_dup_filter(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 {
-	struct cen_bt *bt = hci_get_drvdata(hdev);
 	static const u8 flags;
 	int ret;
 
